#!/usr/bin/python3
"""hearth-claude: Claude (Anthropic) on Hearth OS, installed for you in your home folder.

Claude Desktop for Linux is in beta and Anthropic publishes it as a Debian package (claude-desktop) in its own apt
repository. Hearth OS's system is read-only and only two editions use apt, so on every edition this helper takes
that same package straight from Anthropic, on your device, when you ask for it (Anatase, Peppermint; the code also
copes with the archived Ubuntu and CachyOS editions):
  1. downloads the repository's InRelease and checks its signature with gpg against Anthropic's signing key, pinned
     here by fingerprint (a temporary keyring, nothing is added to yours)
  2. takes the package list's SHA-256 from the signed InRelease and checks the list against it
  3. picks the newest claude-desktop for this machine (amd64 or arm64), downloads it and checks its SHA-256 from
     the list
  4. unpacks it into ~/.local/opt/claude-desktop (dpkg-deb when the system has it; otherwise Python reads the
     .deb itself, as on Anatase) and adds a menu entry, icons, the claude:// link handler (browser sign-in comes back through it)
     and ~/.local/bin/claude-desktop
Nothing is installed system-wide and nothing of Anthropic's ships in Hearth's images. On Anatase this is Anthropic's
Debian build running unofficially (Anthropic supports Debian and Ubuntu; Fedora "coming"). If claude-desktop was
installed through apt (Peppermint), apt owns it: this helper leaves it alone.

The sandbox: Electron's setuid helper (chrome-sandbox) can't be setuid in a home folder, so it's left out and
Chromium uses its user-namespace sandbox instead, which Anatase and Peppermint allow. --no-sandbox is never used; if a system blocks user
namespaces, status says so ("sandbox": false) and the app won't start until they're allowed.

Claude Code (the CLI) is Anthropic's own installer (https://claude.ai/install.sh, run as you): it installs into
~/.local/bin and keeps itself up to date. Sign-in for both is with your claude.ai account, in the browser; this
helper never sees a password, key or token.

  hearth-claude status [--check]   JSON: Desktop and Code; --check also asks Anthropic for the newest Desktop
  hearth-claude install            install (or reinstall) the newest Claude Desktop
  hearth-claude update             install a newer Claude Desktop if Anthropic has one
  hearth-claude remove             remove Claude Desktop (your chats and settings in ~/.config/Claude stay)
  hearth-claude auto-update        what the daily timer runs (hearth-claude-update.timer): update quietly, if
                                   Hearth installed it and it isn't open
  hearth-claude open               start Claude Desktop
  hearth-claude install-code       install Claude Code with Anthropic's installer
  hearth-claude remove-code        remove Claude Code (~/.local/bin/claude, ~/.local/share/claude)
Progress lines "progress: <0-100> <what>", then one JSON line; failures print "error: ..." and exit 1.
"""
